WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Bismillah, alhamdulillah, wa salatu wa salamu
ala rasulullah. Hello, calculus

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:07.670
students. Today we're going to be doing
derivatives using the [ln] function. Let's

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:12.190
get into it. Let's get into our examples.
But first, I want to make sure that we all know

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.550
before we start that the derivative
when y equals ln of x is 1

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.950
over x. But just like our e to the x
case, almost always when

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.110
we're using ln, it's going to be in a chain
rule format because the ln itself is

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.210
already a function. So we're going to put
anything in this function. We're going to

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.970
be using the chain rule. Here, let's use Leibniz
notation to show you what I mean.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:40.290
If we have y equals d of ln of

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:45.530
8x, we're going to have to first take it
over d of 8x and then multiply

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.170
it by d of 8x over d of x.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.250
Taking [the derivative of] the ln of 8x
will give us 1 over 8x,

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.880
just like how taking [the derivative of]
the ln of x will give us 1 over x.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:01:03.840
And then the derivative of 8x equals,
times the derivative of 8x, which is just 8.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:08.240
This will give us, when these 8s
cancel out, still 1 over x.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:16.760
In our next example here, we have f of x
equals ln of 5x cubed plus

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:22.000
3x plus 1. If we take the
derivative of this, we will

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:25.860
again have to take the chain rule. So do the
derivative of the outside multiplied by

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:29.420
the derivative of what's on the inside. The
derivative of the outside with respect

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:34.740
to the g of x function, we get 1
over 5x cubed plus 3x

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.900
plus 1. And then we're going to multiply it by
the derivative of the inside. The

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:44.240
derivative of 5x cubed plus 3x plus
1 is 15x squared plus

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:48.820
3 because that 1 goes to 0. We then get

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:54.120
15x squared plus 3 over 5x cubed

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:59.350
plus 3x plus 1 as our final answer.
On to our third example here, we

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:04.850
have h of x equals ln 2x cubed over x
squared. Here we have a

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:10.010
fraction that follows our quotient rule, so we
can have this as f and this represent

00:02:09.860 --> 00:02:15.450
g, and we know that f over g prime
equals f prime of g minus f

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:20.950
g prime all over g squared. So we can
get our f prime, our g

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:26.210
prime, and then plug them in. Our f prime
of x will be the prime of ln 2x

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:30.720
cubed. We know we're going to have to use the
chain rule, and that will be

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.520
1 over 2x cubed

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:38.140
times the inside derivative, which
will be 6x squared.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:43.280
Here we can simplify. There are [x] cubed here
and x squared here. We can scratch

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:48.320
this out and bring that to a 1, and then this 2
and 6 can become a 3. So we'll get 3

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:53.820
over x. For our g prime of x, that's just going
to be x squared, and [the derivative of] x squared

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:58.980
is 2x. The derivative is 2x. Now we have f prime
and g prime. We can plug them into

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:04.140
our f over g prime. So here we
would get 3 over x

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:08.420
times x squared minus ln of 2x cubed

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:14.760
times 2x all over g squared. g is x squared,
so it's going to be x to the 4.

00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:19.200
We're running out of space here, so I'm going to
move [it] down here. We're going to

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:23.840
multiply 3 over x times x squared. That gives
us 3x. And then we're going to

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:29.040
subtract that 2x ln of 2x cubed

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:34.320
all over x to the power of 4. Here we have
an x and an x and an x that

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.700
can factor out. So that will
give us 3 minus 2 ln

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.850
of 2x cubed all

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:46.870
over x to the power of 3 as our answer.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.610
Again, it's pretty easy. We're just combining
some rules now. But because we know

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:55.690
how to [use] all these tools, it's pretty easy to
get our answers for the derivative.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:04:00.990
The last one here, we have a ln on the outside.
And then, so that's going to be a

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.350
chain rule. And then inside, we have a product
rule. So to begin, we're going to use

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.470
that, we're going to take the derivative of just
the ln with respect to x times e to

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.370
the 2x. So that's going to give us 1 over x e
to the 2x. Then we're going to

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:18.730
multiply the inside with a product rule.
Product rule tells us that we have to do

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:23.050
the first prime multiplied by the second function
times the first function multiplied by

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:28.470
the second prime. When we're
taking x to x prime, or x's

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.650
derivative is 1, so that's 1 times e to
the 2x. And then we're adding

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:38.310
x times the derivative of e to the
2x, which is e to the

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:39.590
2x times 2.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:46.190
Simplifying this a little further, we're going
to get e to the 2x plus 2x e to the

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.150
2x all over x e to the 2x. We can

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:56.630
divide [out] e to the 2x in each of these
terms. We will get 1 plus 2x

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:02.090
over x as our final answer. So
as you can see, this

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:07.550
is not that difficult. We just added one
more step to our process

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:11.790
of solving, and once we have all these tools, these
derivatives become a piece of cake

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:17.290
to be honest. So yeah, the only thing really new
here is just the fact that we know

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:22.770
this identity now, the [derivative of] ln x
equals 1 over x. So if it's involved in a

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.730
question, we're just going to have that as a part
of our chain rule, like we see here,

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:31.130
like we see here, like we see here. And then
this one was a little bit different

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:35.570
because, again, we still did have that chain rule,
but it was an intermediate step. So

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.230
you always have to assess what's on the outside,
what's on the inside, and go from

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.050
there. I will see you in the next one.
